Vendored game-data files
=========================

The following files in this directory are vendored, unmodified, from the
palcalc project:

  db.json        - pal species, passives, active skills, elements, gender probabilities
  breeding.json  - full breeding table + minimum-breeding-steps matrix

Source:  https://github.com/tylercamp/palcalc  (PalCalc.Model/)
Author:  Tyler Camp and palcalc contributors
License: MIT

palcalc is distributed under the MIT License. These data files are included
here under that license as a day-one data contract; pal-calc converts them to
a compact binary pack (pack/paldata.pack) at build time and credits the
original authors. See the palcalc repository for the full license text.

Per-species element types
=========================

  elements.json - internal_name -> [element kinds] (1-2 of the 9 canonical
                  kinds: Normal, Fire, Water, Leaf, Electricity, Ice, Earth,
                  Dark, Dragon), in the game's ElementType1/ElementType2 order.

This is a DERIVED mapping: the element lists were extracted from the
`element_types` field of `data/json/pals.json` and keyed to palcalc's internal
species ids (the game `CharacterID`s that our db.json already uses). It reflects
the current Palworld 1.0 element assignments (e.g. Lovander = Dark, Dumud =
Earth+Water), verified against the game's DT_PalMonsterParameter data table.

Source:  https://github.com/oMaN-Rod/palworld-save-pal  (data/json/pals.json)
Author:  oMaN-Rod and Palworld Save Pal contributors
License: MIT

build-pack merges elements.json into the pack (PalSpecies.elements). The
underlying element facts are game data from Palworld (c) Pocketpair, Inc.,
included here for personal, non-commercial use only.

Icon assets
===========

The pal icons in app/public/pals/ and the element / passive-rank icons in
app/public/elements/ are sourced, unmodified, from palcalc's bundled art
(PalCalc.UI/Resources/Pals, .../Elements, .../TraitRank). pal-calc renames
each pal icon from palcalc's display-name key to the internal species id
(e.g. "Lamball.png" -> "SheepBall.png") but does not alter the image bytes.

The work-suitability icons in app/public/work/ (12 kinds: Kindling, Watering,
Planting, GenerateElectricity, Handiwork, Gathering, Lumbering, Mining,
MedicineProduction, Cooling, Transporting, Farming) are sourced, unmodified,
from palcalc's bundled art (PalCalc.UI/Resources/). The GenerateElectricity
glyph is palcalc's "ElectricityGeneration.png" renamed to match the
WorkSuitability key; the other eleven keep their palcalc filenames.

Source:  https://github.com/tylercamp/palcalc  (PalCalc.UI/Resources/)
Author:  Tyler Camp and palcalc contributors
License: MIT (for palcalc's redistribution)

These images are ultimately game assets from Palworld (c) Pocketpair, Inc.
They are included here for personal, non-commercial use only. All rights to
the underlying artwork remain with Pocketpair.

Per-species partner skills
==========================

  partner-skills.json - internal_name -> { name, description } for each pal's
                        Partner Skill (the game's "PartnerSkill" / "aura").

palcalc's db.json ships PartnerSkill=null for every species, so this is a
DERIVED mapping built from the `aura` { name, description } field of
mlg404/palworld-paldex-api's src/pals.json. Match method: exact (normalized)
English display-name match against palcalc's `Name` (paldex-api's numeric
`id`/`key` is its own sequential index and does NOT align with the game
PalDexNo, so it is not used for matching); slug names like "fluffy_shield" are
title-cased to "Fluffy Shield" (articles/prepositions kept lowercase, e.g.
"Guardian of the Desert"). Elemental variants with no paldex-api entry inherit
their base form's partner skill (game-accurate: Palworld variants share the
base PartnerSkill), resolved via palcalc's `Base_Suffix` internal-name scheme.

Coverage: 169 / 299 species (138 exact name matches + 31 variant->base
inheritances). The remaining ~130 (Sakurajima + Feybreak DLC and the Terraria
collab pals) have no permissive partner-skill source and carry null; the UI
omits the partner-skill section gracefully for those.

Source:  https://github.com/mlg404/palworld-paldex-api  (src/pals.json)
Author:  Victor Eyer and palworld-paldex-api contributors
License: MIT

build-pack merges partner-skills.json into the pack (PalSpecies.partner_skill
and partner_skill_desc). The underlying partner-skill facts are game data from
Palworld (c) Pocketpair, Inc., included here for personal, non-commercial use
only.

Alpha / UI marker icon
======================

The alpha (field-boss) marker in app/public/ui/alpha.png — the red horned icon
shown on alpha pals — is sourced, unmodified in artwork, from palworld-save-pal's
bundled art (ui/src/lib/assets/img/alpha.webp, itself the game's
T_alpha_icon_normal). It was transcoded from WEBP to PNG (pixels unchanged; a
lossless container change only).

